\begin{algorithm}[t]
\caption{Calibration and Two-View Reconstruction}
\label{alg:pipeline}
\small
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\REQUIRE Non-coplanar 3-D controls, corresponding observations for each camera, intrinsic/distortion parameters, and a synchronized stereo observation.
\ENSURE Camera matrices, reconstructed point, reprojection residuals, and acceptance status.
\FOR{each camera $j\in\{1,2\}$}
  \STATE Undistort control observations; reject inversion failures.
  \STATE Compute $T_{2,j}$ and $T_3$ and assemble $A_j$.
  \STATE Compute thin Householder QR, then Jacobi SVD of $R_{A,j}$.
  \STATE Evaluate $\kappa_{\mathrm{nonnull}}$ and $\rho_{\mathrm{null}}$; recover and denormalize $P_j$.
  \STATE Verify gauge admissibility and held-out reprojection error.
\ENDFOR
\STATE Undistort the stereo observation and assemble $M\X=\mathbf{b}$.
\STATE Solve by Householder QR; calculate $\kappaTwo$, camera centres, and $\theta_{\mathrm{ray}}$.
\STATE Calculate reprojection residuals in the matching image-coordinate domain.
\IF{all numerical, ray-angle, and reprojection gates pass}
  \RETURN $\hat{\X}$ and \textsc{Accepted}.
\ELSE
  \RETURN $\hat{\X}$ with diagnostic flags and \textsc{Rejected}.
\ENDIF
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\section{Implementation and Numerical Evaluation}
\subsection{Implementation and Cross-Implementation Agreement}
The numerical core is implemented in double-precision Java, with a TypeScript/V8 implementation used as a reference for selected calculations. Preallocated workspaces reuse primitive buffers for calibration and triangulation operations, reducing avoidable allocation in the numerical kernels. This design is compatible with local/offline video analysis; however, throughput and garbage-collection claims require profiling on a specified computer, video format, frame rate, and workload and are not inferred from numerical parity alone.

